Retro gets the contrast it was missing
======================================

Sampled from the running window, the palette was correct and the interface still read as washed out:

    body/background  68% of the window    correct
    sidebar          19%                  correct
    panels            7%                  correct
    accent           present, #02d63a     correct

What was wrong was the middle of the ramp. `--muted` sat at #5c8a66 (33% saturation) and carried most
of the labels, helper text, card subtitles and inactive nav, so everything secondary collapsed into
the background. `--line` at #0d2312 was too close to the panel colour to read as a border, and
`--raised` at #111911 is neutral — next to a green shell it reads blue-grey, which is what made the
composer controls look like they belonged to a different theme.

  muted   #5c8a66 -> #7fb18c
  line    #0d2312 -> #17492a
  raised  #111911 -> #13251a

The heading is the accent now instead of body white, matching how the reference palette uses green for
anything that carries meaning. Body prose stays #d9d9d9 so long answers remain readable.

diff -Naur a/resources/ui/app.css b/resources/ui/app.css
